{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide an additional dwelling, it fails to provide an acceptable quality of accommodation,&nbsp; would cause a loss of local amenity including to neighbouring occupiers, and would not be located in an area with a high level of access to public transport. As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s supply of family housing and is contrary to the following policies:&nbsp;- National Planning Policy Framework (December 2024)-&nbsp;Policies&nbsp;D6, D14 and T4&nbsp;of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP3, SP8, DMD1, DMT1, DMH5 and DMSI3&nbsp;of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;The&amp;nbsp;proposed flat would fail&amp;nbsp;to comply with the internal space standards for a 1-bed 1-person flat and 2-bed 3-person flat and would result in the provision of&amp;nbsp; sub-standard quality of accommodation.&amp;nbsp;This&amp;nbsp;is unacceptable and contrary to the following:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policy D6,&amp;nbsp; Policy H1 and H2 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Policy SP3, DMD 1 and Part 6 of policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 11pt;&quot;&gt;Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;",
    "The proposal fails to&nbsp;demonstrate that the development would have capacity to facilitate and adequately-sized bin and bike storage areas which are functional, well-located and secure. The proposal lacks clarity and is therefore is unacceptable and contrary to the following: - Policy T5 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policy&nbsp;DMT3 and&nbsp;Part 3 in policy DMSI 8&nbsp;of the Local Plan (September 2024)-&nbsp;The Council&#39;s Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments (dated 20/05/2021)."
  ],
